  "output": {
    "answer": "That flapping was from my own instrumented session, not a real viewer's reaction. On September 2nd I ran my first instrumented live session, and on screen the scout was locking onto a card and letting go at least once a second — jittery, not close to usable, even though the identification underneath was working. That's the only account in the record: me watching my own build on a live stream, not a separate user's response. I don't have anything documenting how an actual outside viewer perceived it during that run.",
